IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spc-nouns`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, dates and ages the text states.
--
-- DATES ARE DATA. Every date and age figure the Act states is a named value
-- with its @ref; the commencement dates the text leaves to an order are inputs.
--
-- THE DATE OF ENACTMENT IS NOT IN THE DEPOSITED TEXT. The file starts with the
-- title, the chapter number ("2002 c. 16") and the long title; it carries no date
-- of Royal Assent in square brackets and no assent date anywhere. The brief asks
-- for the enactment date as a defined value; the text does not give one and none
-- is supplied from memory. `the date of Royal Assent, as the deposited text
-- states it` is therefore NOTHING (a MAYBE DATE), asserted so in the tests, and
-- the rule that needs the day (section 22(2)) takes it as an input.

§ `State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- dates and ages the text states`

§§ `Title page: the date of enactment`

-- src:1 | State Pension Credit Act 2002
-- src:2 | 2002 c. 16
@ref Title and chapter number (src:1-2)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date of Royal Assent, as the deposited text states it` MEANS NOTHING

§§ `Section 22: short title, commencement and extent`

-- src:378 | (1) This Act may be cited as the State Pension Credit Act 2002.
-- src:379 | (2) This section and sections 19 and 20 come into force on the passing of this Act.
-- src:380 | (3) Except as provided by subsection (2), this Act shall come into force on such day as the Secretary of State may by order appoint; and different days may be so appointed for different purposes.
@ref s 22(2), (3) (src:378-380)
GIVEN `the day of Royal Assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 22(2) -- this section and sections 19 and 20 come into force on` `the day of Royal Assent` MEANS
    `the day of Royal Assent`

-- Section 22(3): "such day as the Secretary of State may by order appoint; and
-- different days may be so appointed for different purposes." The Act fixes no
-- day, so the day appointed for the purpose in hand is an input, and the question
-- "is the provision in force on this day" is a comparison.
@ref s 22(3) (src:380)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day appointed by order for that purpose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) -- a provision brought into force by order is in force on` day `if the day appointed for it is` `the day appointed by order for that purpose` MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the day appointed by order for that purpose`

§§ `Section 22(6): extent`

-- Section 22(6) says the Act extends to England and Wales and Scotland only,
-- and section 1(2)(a) asks whether the claimant is in Great Britain. They are two
-- statements about one territory; the extent clause decides nothing for a person.
-- src:383 | (6) Subject to that, this Act extends to England and Wales and Scotland only.
@ref s 22(6) (src:383)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 22(6) -- the extent of the Act` MEANS
    "England and Wales and Scotland only"

§§ `The calendar dates the Act states`

-- Section 3(1)(a): "has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016".
-- Also section 3ZA(2) and (3), and section 6(1).
-- src:48 | (a) has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65 (before, on or after that date), or
@ref s 3(1)(a) (src:48)
GIVETH A DATE
`6 April 2016` MEANS YearMonthDay 2016 4 6

-- Section 9(6): an assessed income period "brought to an end, on or after 6 April
-- 2009 but before 6 April 2014". The window is closed at its start and open at its end.
-- src:154 | (a) an assessed income period is brought to an end , on or after 6 April 2009 but before 6 April 2014, by the expiry of a period of 5 years or more, and
@ref s 9(6)(a) (src:154)
GIVETH A DATE
`6 April 2009` MEANS YearMonthDay 2009 4 6

@ref s 9(6)(a) (src:154)
GIVETH A DATE
`6 April 2014` MEANS YearMonthDay 2014 4 6

§§ `The ages the Act states`

-- Section 3(1)(a), 6(3)(c) and 9(4)(c), (d): the age of 65.
-- src:48 | (a) has attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and has attained the age of 65 (before, on or after that date), or
@ref s 3(1)(a) (src:48)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of 65` MEANS 65

-- Section 9(1): under 75 on the day the relevant decision takes effect, or 75 or over.
-- src:141 | (a) in the case of a claimant who is under the age of 75 on the day on which the relevant decision takes effect, the period of 5 years beginning with that day;
-- src:142 | (b) in the case of a claimant who is aged 75 or over on that day, an indefinite period beginning with that day.
@ref s 9(1)(a), (b) (src:141-142)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of 75` MEANS 75

-- Section 9(6)(b): "the claimant is aged 80 or over".
-- src:155 | (b) the claimant is aged 80 or over at that time,
@ref s 9(6)(b) (src:155)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of 80` MEANS 80

-- Section 9(1)(a): "the period of 5 years beginning with that day".
@ref s 9(1)(a) (src:141)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 5 years of an assessed income period` MEANS 5

§§ `Attaining an age (section 17(3))`

-- Section 17(3) applies section 173 of the Contributions and Benefits Act
-- ("meaning of attaining an age etc"). That section is NOT among the inputs. The
-- encoding takes an age to be attained on the anniversary of the day of birth
-- (the fork is registered in NOTES.md, F-04). For a birth on 29 February, the
-- lenient `Date` constructor carries the anniversary in a year with no 29 February
-- to 1 March (probed on the stable l4: Date 29 2 2017 is 1 March 2017).
-- src:314 | (3) The following provisions of the Contributions and Benefits Act, namely—
-- src:315 | (a) section 172 (references to Great Britain or United Kingdom to include reference to adjacent territorial waters etc), and
-- src:316 | (b) section 173 (meaning of attaining an age etc),
-- src:317 | shall apply for the purposes of this Act as they apply for the purposes of that Act.
@ref s 17(3) (src:314-317)
GIVEN `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which the age is attained` `date of birth` age MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY `date of birth`) (DATE_MONTH `date of birth`) (DATE_YEAR `date of birth` PLUS age)

@ref s 17(3) (src:314-317)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the age has been attained on` day `by a person born on` `date of birth` `at the age of` age MEANS
    day AT LEAST `the day on which the age is attained` `date of birth` age
